# Prompt Conventions

## All prompts live in the prompts module

Every LLM prompt must live under `src/common/prompts/<group>/` as a Handlebars template paired with a Zod schema, and be registered in `prompts.registry.ts`. Never inline prompt strings inside services, controllers, or tools.

```
src/common/prompts/
  <group>/
    system.hbs         # template
    system.schema.ts   # Zod schema (default export)
  prompts.registry.ts  # add the new key here
```

## One group per LLM call

A `<group>` represents a single, self-contained LLM call (one feature / one model invocation). Files inside a group only differ by the role they play in that one call: `system.hbs` for the system prompt, `user.hbs` for the user prompt — never by feature.

If you find yourself adding a second, unrelated prompt to an existing group (e.g. a summarization step next to a chat completion), create a new group instead. Group names should describe the call, not the surrounding domain.

```
# ❌ BAD — two unrelated LLM calls share the `chat` group
src/common/prompts/
  chat/
    system.hbs    # system prompt for the chat completion
    summary.hbs   # ← different LLM call (summarization), wrong place

# ✅ GOOD — each LLM call gets its own group
src/common/prompts/
  chat/
    system.hbs        # chat completion
  chatSummary/
    system.hbs        # summarization call
```

Registry keys mirror this: `chat/system`, `chatSummary/system` — not `chat/summary`.

## Render via PromptsService

Services must inject `PromptsService` and call `render(key, input)`. Never call `streamText`/`generateText` (or similar) with a string literal in `system` or `prompt`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — prompt inlined in the service
return streamText({
  model: `${character.provider}/${character.model}`,
  system: `You are ${character.firstName}. You are at ${place.name}...`,
  messages,
});

// ❌ BAD — prompt template kept in a local constant or sibling file
const SYSTEM_PROMPT = `You are {{character.firstName}}...`;

// ✅ GOOD — template + schema in src/common/prompts, rendered via the service
return streamText({
  model: `${character.provider}/${character.model}`,
  system: this.promptsService.render('chat/system', {
    character,
    place,
    user,
  }),
  messages,
});
```

## Adding a new prompt — checklist

1. Create `src/common/prompts/<group>/<name>.hbs` with the Handlebars template.
2. Create `src/common/prompts/<group>/<name>.schema.ts` exporting a `z.object({...})` as the default export.
3. Register it in `src/common/prompts/prompts.registry.ts`:

```typescript
export const promptRegistry = {
  'place/system': placeSystemPromptSchema,
  'chat/system': chatSystemPromptSchema,
  'mynew/system': myNewSystemPromptSchema,
} as const satisfies Record<string, z.ZodObject>;
```

4. Import `PromptsModule` in the consumer module and inject `PromptsService` to render it.
